FIVE SELF-CAUGHT DEFECTS IN THIS SUITE, FIXED AT BIRTH
  (a) AC-BSRB3 compared os.listdir to a fixed list, so directory order alone
      reddened it - now sorted() on both sides;
  (b) the tamper matcher used exact list membership, but the tool appends
      ":<family>" to drift tokens, so five of six controls read as absent -
      now matched by prefix, the same law the shipped do_control uses;
  (c) AC-BSRB7 and AC-BSRB8 inherited that exact-match bug and now share one
      prefix helper;
  (d) the banned-import needle table matched ITSELF (the needles are literals
      in this file) - six false positives; needles are now assembled from
      fragments, the same self-match trap the fleet process probes hit;
  (e) sorted() was applied to one side only in the first repair.  No criterion
      was relaxed by any of these: every fix made the check stricter or
      correct.

